---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How Knowledge Hub behaves for keyboard, screen reader, reduced motion, and zoom, including what is not done yet."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="prose-page page-width" tabindex="-1">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
    <h1>How this site behaves</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      The target is WCAG 2.2 AA. This page describes what is actually
      implemented and tested, and what is not, rather than claiming compliance
      in general.
    </p>

    <h2>Animation</h2>
    <p>
      Every lesson opens with an animation that starts on its own and repeats.
      One control pauses it and holds the current state; pressing it again
      continues from there rather than starting over.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your device asks for reduced motion, the animation never starts. The
      opening state is held, the control is hidden because there is no motion to
      control, and the full step-by-step sequence below carries the same
      explanation. The animation also suspends while it is scrolled out of view
      or the tab is hidden.
    </p>

    <h2>Meaning never depends on one channel</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing is conveyed by color, motion, or position alone. Every animated
      state has a written description, and the complete step sequence is
      rendered as static figures with text, so the lesson is readable whether or
      not the animation runs at all. If the animation fails to load, the notice
      explains it and the rest of the lesson is untouched.
    </p>

    <h2>Keyboard and screen readers</h2>
    <p>
      Every control is reachable by keyboard with a visible focus indicator, and
      there are no focus traps. A skip link leads straight to the main content.
      Headings run in order with one level-one heading per page. The animation
      does not announce each loop to a screen reader, which would otherwise
      interrupt continuously.
    </p>

    <h2>Zoom and reflow</h2>
    <p>
      The layout reflows at 200% zoom without a horizontal scrollbar and without
      clipping content. The step sequence scrolls sideways inside its own
      region, which is a deliberate one-dimensional scroll rather than the page
      scrolling in two directions.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site stores nothing in your browser: no cookies, no local storage, no
      session storage. This is asserted by an automated test, not assumed.
    </p>

    <h2>What is tested, and how</h2>
    <p>
      Automated accessibility checks run against every pull request across the
      lesson's opening, terminal, paused, expanded, and reduced-motion states,
      alongside keyboard traversal and reflow checks. Anything reported as
      serious or critical fails the build.
    </p>

    <h2>Known gaps</h2>
    <p>Stated plainly rather than left for you to discover:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Automated checks run in Chromium only. Firefox and WebKit are not yet
        covered.
      </li>
      <li>
        Screen-reader behavior has been checked by hand rather than
        continuously, so a regression there would not be caught automatically.
      </li>
      <li>
        Visual regression baselines exist but are not enforced in continuous
        integration.
      </li>
      <li>
        The animation labels inside lesson figures are small on narrow screens.
        They scale with the figure and are readable, but they are the tightest
        thing on the page.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Accessibility problems are the most useful issues to report. Please say
      what you were using, what you expected, and what happened. The repository
      is linked in the footer.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
    padding-block: var(--section-space);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-accent-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
  }

  .lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-9) var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed, 1.7);
  }

  p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-5);
  }

  ul {
    display: grid;
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-7);
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
